Blei

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.370
Edel

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.370
Dünste

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.240
That's all. You are dismissed.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.010
You're there like the wind

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.640
Closing your eyes at sunset

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.270
I wonder what's on your mind

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.610
Beyond Journey's End

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.990
With your eyelids open

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.580
Your eyes shone like glass

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:08.330
It faintly smelled like a sunny day

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:19.470
Clear up the sky, let flowers bloom

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.680
Bloom and blame it on the sunny sky

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.060
Even the rain, when it stops

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:33.070
Will make you shine in the sunlight

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:38.450
Calm the stirring sounds in my heart

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.490
We go like the sunny wind

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.910
Go on and fly over that cloud

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.750
Further and further away

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:58.010
Episode 22: Future Enemies

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.350
It's evening, huh?

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.450
Lazing around isn't half bad.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.370
What's going on?

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.650
Coming.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.800
Fern? I thought you were at 
the first-class mage exam.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.340
The first test is over. 
We returned last night.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.890
Mr. Stark, you know it's evening, don't you?

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:57.680
What?

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.410
You were asleep, weren't you?

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.520
Did you stay up all night?

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:08.410
Yes.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:09.920
What else?

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.290
I drank juice in the middle of the night.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.640
Sorry! I'm sorry, okay?

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.160
Uh-oh. You made her angry.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.200
Ms. Frieren, you only just woke up, too.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.610
Caught in the crossfire.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.590
Looks like we'll be spending 
the day making Fern happy.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.480
What should we do?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.330
Let's get something good to eat.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.800
Something good?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.750
It's a bit expensive,

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.570
but I found a nice place when I came here 
before with Himmel and the others.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.550
Wasn't that over eighty years ago? 
Will it still be there?

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.800
Oh, my.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.250
The lantern lit up.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.430
I told you it was an easy fix.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.330
Thank you as always, Richter.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.180
Sure thing.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.410
I know. You're welcome to have these.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.190
I'll see you later.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.450
Grandma, I'm not a kid anymore.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.430
I'm a middle-aged man.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.950
To an old woman like me, 
you're still a child.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.960
You like those, don't you?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.370
Sorry, but the shop is closed.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.730
A crazy old man dragged me into a fistfight.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.540
I need to rest.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.340
Sounds rough, Richter.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.940
Why don't we get something 
to eat together, then?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.280
There's a restaurant we're looking for,

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.130
but Laufen and I don't know the area.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.010
Laufen, what are you doing 
with Denken, anyway?

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.140
And where'd you get that thing you're eating?

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.230
The old man bought these for me.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.520
I'm not sharing.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.230
What are you, his granddaughter?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.020
Now, leave. We're no longer a party.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.310
You don't know how to get 
along in the world, do you?

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:44.690
If you intend to live as a mage, then 
ingratiating yourself to me wouldn't hurt.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.370
There are plenty of places 
to eat around here.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.670
Just choose one.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.800
My wife and I...

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.630
Before she passed away, 
we visited a restaurant together.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.100
I've never forgotten the taste of their food.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.510
You'd better be paying.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.930
Of course I am.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.820
I told you, it can't hurt.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.840
Four-eyes.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.750
Übel.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.560
It's nice to finally meet you.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.130
You don't use a clone when you're in town?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.750
If you just want to make small talk, 
do you mind if we walk?

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.170
That's fine, but if you try to run 
away from me, I might kill you.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.670
Can I ask you something?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:07.140
You don't think anything 
of killing people, do you?

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.230
Why didn't you kill Wirbel?

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:14.000
You had the opportunity, didn't you?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.690
You were watching?

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:18.530
Nothing gets past you, huh?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.540
It's hard to explain.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.410
I'm surprised.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:32.550
Your hands are already drenched in blood,
and yet you still want to remain human.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.330
That's right. I use this time 
to prepare myself to kill.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.320
Maybe it's because I empathized with him.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.770
It made me want to put off 
the killing blow, too.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:53.250
I can't move. What is this?

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.460
Sorganeil.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.070
It's a spell that binds whoever I'm looking at.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:04.590
The magic a person specializes in 
is strongly related to their life and nature.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.340
I've always been this way.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.760
Empathizing with someone 
allows me to use their spells,

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.580
and I can't use the spells of anyone 
I can't empathize with.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.320
Four-eyes, your clones are such 
perfect copies of yourself

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.480
that they're capable of everything you are.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.030
What goes through that head of yours? 
What kind of life have you led?

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.450
Tell me.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.490
I see.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.060
You use magic by feel.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:42.630
The type of mage who casts spells without 
understanding the principles behind them.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.380
I don't like dim-witted people like you.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.250
That doesn't answer my question.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.470
I'm saying I won't tell you 
because I don't like you.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.410
I don't mind if you kill me,

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:06.010
though you'll never get another chance 
to empathize with me if you do.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:18.360
I'll pass. I think I understand you 
a little better now.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.190
Oh?

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.770
I think I'd like to know more.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:28.030
Where were you headed?

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.920
Who knows? Don't follow me.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.800
This is it.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.040
You've got a good eye, Denken.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.300
This is the best restaurant in town.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.320
I come here all the time.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:46.850
My wife and I visited 
this place fifty years ago.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.370
Looks like it hasn't changed.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.520
How curious.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.710
Really?

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.030
You're sure I can order 
as many desserts as I want?

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:04.960
Sure.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.470
Denken, it's Frieren.

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:09.740
What should I get?

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.420
I recommend...

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:14.990
It's not my birthday. 
Can I really indulge myself like this?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.990
Leave them be. They look 
like they're having fun.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.970
Meals should be enjoyed.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.640
We're here for the same reason, after all.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.120
All right. Time to stuff myself.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.940
That's a ton of food, huh?

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.380
Ms. Frieren, you like to eat like 
this sometimes, don't you?

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:53.410
Thank you for returning the heirloom knife 
the demons took from me.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.270
I, Lecker, the greatest chef of the century,

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:01.880
shall provide you with the ultimate service 
and reward you however I can.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.780
That's a lot of food, isn't it?

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:07.350
The food here is good.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.320
We'd better savor everything we can.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.550
You still don't need to eat so much at once.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.030
There's always next time.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:18.020
I thought so, too, but there are many flavors 
I've never been able to experience again.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.770
Don't worry, Ms. Frieren.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:28.480
This restaurant's flavors will live on 
through future generations.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:31.300
They'll still be around 100 
or even 200 years from now.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:39.010
I see. It's interesting, isn't it? 
All chefs say that.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:43.680
Then they try to leave their mark 
by changing the flavors of past dishes.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:50.050
If that happens, we can simply find 
even more delicious flavors.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:56.110
Forgive me, Mr. Himmel, but there are 
no flavors in this world greater than mine.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.820
Then you'd better make sure 
they last into the future.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.700
That's the reward I ask for this job.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:14.050
If that is your wish, Hero, then I shall do 
what no chef has done before.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.770
Frieren, this is really good!

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:26.370
Does anyone deserve to be this happy?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.890
Seriously? Despite all he said, 
the flavors have changed.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:44.560
But now I don't have to 
look for tastier flavors.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.180
It's way better now than it was back then.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:56.060
It really is good.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.940
You have food on your cheek, Mr. Stark.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.990
You must eat your vegetables, too.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.420
You're totally acting like her grandfather.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.080
Huh. You're a lighter eater than I expected.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.080
What's wrong with that?

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.780
That was delicious, Ms. Frieren.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.030
I'm glad she's in a better mood.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.780
By the way, how's our money situation?

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.510
I used up my savings.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.010
This is the state of nothingness.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:37.430
You've arrived at the essence of martial arts.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:42.580
There is nothing left for me to teach you.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.960
Who was that old man?

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.080
I don't know.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.600
He comes to talk to me when I'm training.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:03.210
You seem to attract a lot of weird people.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.080
Well, whatever. Do you have a minute?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.120
I'd like your help with something.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.820
What happened?

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.280
The heck? She's super pissed off.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.460
She's in an even worse mood than yesterday.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.120
I know.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:21.210
What did you do?

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:25.840
It was my turn to go shopping today, 
but I overslept.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.890
You do that all the time. 
Why would she get mad about it now?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.810
Fern is the type to let things 
build up until she explodes.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.890
What happens when she explodes?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.240
She gives me the silent treatment.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.360
Do you have to fight like children?

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:44.970
Please, Stark. I need you to mediate for us.

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.790
She won't talk to me.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:51.590
What? No way. I'm too scared.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.760
You're right. Sorry. 
That was an unreasonable ask.

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:09.280
Listen, Ms. Fern. 
She's sorry for what she did.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:11.980
I want to eat.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:12.670
What?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.620
I want to eat snacks.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.820
She's such a pain in the butt.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.440
Then let's go buy some together.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.750
I wonder if I've got any savings left.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.600
Huh? Isn't he...

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.830
Wirbel of the Northern Magic Corps, right?

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.610
You're a warrior, aren't you?

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:49.480
Huh? What do you want?

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:50.440
What do you think?

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.770
Huh? What?

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.460
He won't do.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.610
I wonder what he's up to.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.500
Thanks for waiting, Kanne.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:11.020
You're looking cuter than ever, Lawine.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:14.880
My brothers are home 
from the imperial capital.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:21.090
They always buy crap I don't need.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:23.990
I'm not their dress-up doll.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.380
My mom's really into it, too.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.380
She made no effort to stop them.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:33.310
You're even more spoiled than me.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.930
If that's what you think, 
then let's trade places.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.380
It's hell being compared 
to my talented brothers.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:42.850
Come on, let's go. This outfit is so stifling.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:51.690
Then allow me to escort you today, 
Little Miss Lawine.

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:01.040
Ow, ow! You're gonna rip them off!

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:26.170
Um, Ms. Fern. What would you like?

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:30.770
Anything is fine. You can choose, Mr. Stark.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.370
She only says that when 
she wants something specific.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.680
What should we do?

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:41.040
Don't ask me.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.180
Hey, isn't that Frieren?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:48.060
Yeah.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.380
I'm glad we ran into you.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.330
We were just thinking about 
visiting you at the inn.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.170
Who are they?

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.790
We were in the same party 
during the first test.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:06.020
Frieren was really helpful.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.740
Also, she was like a teacher.

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.770
Oh?

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.820
Because you two wouldn't stop fighting.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.460
It's Lawine's fault.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.790
Ow, ow!

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:18.120
I don't feel comfortable 
being surrounded by girls.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.730
Now, now.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.200
Hey.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:19.860
What?

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.790
You're a warrior, aren't you?

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:22.610
Huh?

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.610
What? H-Hey...

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.230
Stop. Wh-What's this about?

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.950
You're great.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.800
What's going on?!

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:36.260
The Continental Magic Association

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:40.370
has hired me to eliminate a Fresser 
that's been ravaging crops.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.170
I'm looking for a front-liner.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.510
We met during the test, right?

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:47.280
Is he your friend? Can I borrow him?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.100
Go right ahead.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.200
How could you?!

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:53.340
How could you?

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.420
He's taking your friend away. 
Are you okay with this?

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:58.180
It'll be fine. He had no ill intentions.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.560
I could hardly believe he was the same person.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.840
He's probably the type who can 
turn it on and off for work.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.370
My brothers are like that, too.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:09.300
Here, Frieren.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.150
Thank you.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.880
I didn't do anything to deserve your thanks.

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:17.750
No.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:22.810
If not for you, we wouldn't have 
advanced to the second test.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:23.940
Thank you.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.770
Thank you, Mr. Himmel.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:32.710
There's nothing to worry about now.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:33.480
Yeah.

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.680
Go on. Your parents are waiting for you.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:37.570
Okay.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.710
Himmel, why do you help people?

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:49.190
Because I'm a hero.

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:51.030
That's not what I meant.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:57.980
Well, maybe I do it for myself.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:04.040
Maybe it's because I want 
people to remember me.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:12.980
To live is to be known 
and remembered by others.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:18.060
What should I do to be remembered?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:24.260
Change someone's life, 
even just in a small way.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.290
That's probably enough.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:40.200
Anyway, then Lawine...

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.480
No, that was you, Kanne.

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.280
What? Is that right?

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.250
There was that other time, too. Remember?

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:53.880
Ms. Frieren, these sweets 
they gave us are really good.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.860
You're finally feeling better.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:21:00.640
Come to think of it, Frieren struggled 
to get up on the morning of the second day.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:04.560
Don't talk about that. 
You'll sour her mood again.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:06.060
Hmph.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:07.790
Frieren.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:13.030
Typically, the first-class mage exam 
consists of three tests.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:15.040
Next time, we'll be enemies.

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:16.540
That's true.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.170
What's that?

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.930
It's a notification of the next test.

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:32.760
There's the location and date 
of the second test,

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:36.040
as well as the proctor's name.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:39.950
The proctor is Sense, huh? 
Our luck just ran out.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:43.200
Aw, man. And after we passed 
the first test and everything.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.820
What do you mean?

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:49.840
Sense has proctored four tests in the past.

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:52.950
Not a single person passed any of them.

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:25.280
This meat is good.

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:29.080
You're incredible. You demonstrated 
the essence of martial arts!

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:36.800
You've put together a dreadful test.

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:39.800
You think so?

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:43.130
I'm a pacifist, Genau,

00:22:45.570 --> 00:22:47.680
unlike you.

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.140
And I'm alright (I'll be alright)

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.060
Yeah, I hear you (I care about you)

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:01.650
The wind teases this hair that's longer now

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:04.070
There's meaning in everything

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.070
Even the days that came to a halt

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:13.700
Now that I finally understand,
I've caught up to you

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:17.500
See, things that couldn't have been

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.370
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:25.050
Why? They begin to overflow

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:31.300
I won't ask to see you, so at least

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:37.060
Let me remember the past, just for today

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:43.060
So, if we were to meet again

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:48.940
No more hesitations, I'd choose the present

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.990
Anytime, anywhere, yah (wherever you are)

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:57.620
Anytime, anywhere (smile for me)

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.620
I'll be there (close your eyes,
and I'll always be there)

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.380
Even if there are no absolutes

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:06.420
I'm always aware of your thoughts

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:12.470
Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:19.390
I'm whispering our lullaby
for you to come back home

00:24:19.960 --> 00:24:22.690
I wasn't expecting to encounter these here.

00:24:20.710 --> 00:24:21.800
It's a gargoyle!

00:24:21.800 --> 00:24:23.190
It's a mimic.

00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:24.440
Brutal. It doesn't even leave bones behind.

00:24:22.710 --> 00:24:24.520
I can't agree to that.

00:24:23.210 --> 00:24:25.260
It must be the work of demons or monsters.

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:26.610
We'll proceed with caution 
while mapping the dungeon.

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:27.680
They must be terrifyingly powerful.

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:29.980
Episode 23







Conquering the Labyrinth

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:30.060
For the second test, 
you will be raiding a dungeon.
